From: Linxira OS <admin@linxira.org>
Subject: [PATCH] initcpiocfg: drop obsolete crc32c-intel module

Linux resolves the CRC32C implementation through module dependencies. The
explicit Intel module was removed from current kernels, so adding it makes
mkinitcpio fail on Intel systems using Btrfs.

--- a/src/modules/initcpiocfg/main.py
+++ b/src/modules/initcpiocfg/main.py
@@ -241,9 +241,7 @@ def find_initcpio_features(partitions, root_mount_point):
     else:
         hooks.extend(["filesystems"])
 
-    if uses_btrfs:
-        modules.append("crc32c-intel" if cpuinfo().is_intel else "crc32c")
-    else:
+    if not uses_btrfs:
         hooks.append("fsck")
 
     # Modify according to the keys in the configuration
